Save a posted video under its subject
	:comment Problem: FB wants login + browser TLS
	:comment Approach: escalate yt-dlp strategies
	Take a URL or a list of URLs
		:if Is the argument a .txt file?
			Download each URL in it@$ fbdl urls.txt
		:else
			Download the one URL@$ fbdl <URL>
	Choose the downloader
		:if Audio or subtitles only?
			Use yt-dlp alone@$ fbdl <URL> -a / --subs / -S
		:else
			Try yt-dlp, then fall back@to the built-in scraper
	Escalate cookies x TLS impersonation
		Stop at the first success@(order depends on the site)
	Name the file by its subject
		YYYYMMDD_<subject>, from a@declared title or claude -p
		Save the post body as .txt@(first line: source URL)
	:while Are older downloads misnamed?
		Person previews the renames@$ fbdl-rename -n
		Rename video, .txt and .srt@$ fbdl-rename
	:terminal Videos named by what they show
